# Matchup generation

Page load **checks for a stored guide first**. If one exists, show it. If not, show the modelled read and generate in the background (`ensureMatchupGuide`). Do not block the response on OpenAI.

## Model

Judgment copy uses `gpt-5.6-sol` + `reasoning_effort: "high"`. Verdict, score, and difficulty stay computed in code (`matchupVerdict`). Do not ask the model who wins.

## Spend

Reserve a slot in `matchup_generation_usage` **before** the OpenAI call. Defaults: 2 in flight, 8/hour, 40/day. `OPENAI_MATCHUP_GENERATION=off` is a kill switch. Fail closed on a missing key. Same pairing is generated once (`kit_hash`); number-only patches reuse punish/trade copy unless a rework/new ability lands.

## Editorial rules

Player-facing constraints live in `MATCHUP_GUIDE_RULES` in `apps/api/src/generate-matchup.ts`. Append a line there when policy changes, then bump `MATCHUP_PROMPT_VERSION` so existing guides refresh. Do not invent items, runes, or pairwise samples. Write only from the locked `you` champion — Garen vs Darius is not Darius vs Garen.

## Do not

- Pregenerate the full champion grid
- Raise model/effort “to be safe”
- Let a page view bypass the budget reserve
- Treat the Coaching “Generate” button as matchup generation (it only restates the snapshot)
